\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces This plot illustrates the average value of production by age, across a variety of different metrics, smoothed by a LOESS estimator. Note that for a specific individual, we see metrics heavily adhere to prior beliefs of aging. There still exist upward ticks for certain metrics, but players tend to have lower minutes played toward the end of their careers, so those upticks could be due to random chance, illustrating the need to model heteroscedasticity. We see the wide variety in peak location, peak value, and pre/post-peak behavior across metrics, as well as across players. Rate metrics are presented on a per 36 minutes basis for easier interpretation. \relax }}{6}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:empirical_production_players}{{1}{6}{This plot illustrates the average value of production by age, across a variety of different metrics, smoothed by a LOESS estimator. Note that for a specific individual, we see metrics heavily adhere to prior beliefs of aging. There still exist upward ticks for certain metrics, but players tend to have lower minutes played toward the end of their careers, so those upticks could be due to random chance, illustrating the need to model heteroscedasticity. We see the wide variety in peak location, peak value, and pre/post-peak behavior across metrics, as well as across players. Rate metrics are presented on a per 36 minutes basis for easier interpretation. \relax }{figure.caption.1}{}}
