\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces This plot illustrates the average value of production by age, across a variety of different metrics, smoothed by a LOESS estimator. Note that some of these estimates do not respect aging beliefs (i.e some metrics indicate infinite improvement with respect to age, as well as a decrease then improvement). This observation can be explained by selection bias; players who are more successful are likely to play later in their careers, and tend to have higher values of production, biasing curves upwards. \relax }}{54}{figure.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:empirical_production}{{19}{54}{This plot illustrates the average value of production by age, across a variety of different metrics, smoothed by a LOESS estimator. Note that some of these estimates do not respect aging beliefs (i.e some metrics indicate infinite improvement with respect to age, as well as a decrease then improvement). This observation can be explained by selection bias; players who are more successful are likely to play later in their careers, and tend to have higher values of production, biasing curves upwards. \relax }{figure.caption.36}{}}
